 "notes": "Top-down grasp controller. Palm faces down, fingers point forward, and the hand yaw (psi) is aligned to the cube's yaw mod 90\u00b0. At start it picks an aligned psi from a set of candidates. A candidate must be reachable by IK at the grasp and hover heights, and it should keep the fingertips out of the bin walls. If every aligned candidate collides with a bin, it tilts the hand up by 0.2 rad and raises the grasp height by 1.2 cm. Cartesian-step damped-least-squares IK drives the arm, with nullspace pull toward the grasp posture. Phases: hover over the cube, descend behind it, slide 2.4 cm forward so the thumb clears the cube, close over 0.8 s, lift, then carry. The carry is a synchronized joint-space move to a precomputed IK posture above the target bin. Then it lowers, opens and retreats. Results: about 39/40 on practice seeds 100000-100039 and 28/30 on seeds 100100-100129. Known weaknesses: cubes close to the body at x\u22480.18-0.19, y\u2248-0.11..-0.14, where IK has no good palm-down solution or the wrist hits its limit; cubes near the bin walls, where a finger can push the cube; and slip during the carry's hand rotation when the grasp yaw is far from 0. The controller relies on observed cube positions and has no regrasp or retry logic.",
